   "html_text": "Any attempt to understand Fechner must come to terms with both sides of his personality. We must do justice to his panpsychism as well as his positivism. We can dismiss the panpsychism on positivist grounds, as many have done; but if we do that, we beg questions against Fechner. He insisted that his conclusions are based on well-grounded inferences from facts of experience, and he pointed out (rightly) that resistance to his views was often based on little more than prejudice. Far from a reckles",
